WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 1.6 · Strategic Foundations
Positioning and comparative advantage

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Answer one question: why you, rather than someone else, or no one?

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:28.504
Positioning is the specific place your initiative will take in its landscape: the need, the people, your approach and why you are well placed. It answers one question: why you, rather than someone else, or no one?

4
00:00:28.904 --> 00:00:29.504
Three parts of a position

5
00:00:29.504 --> 00:00:40.463
Your focus: The need you focus on, the people you serve and your approach. For example: Maths tutoring for teenagers in one district whose families cannot afford private lessons.

6
00:00:40.463 --> 00:00:51.793
Your advantage: Why you are well placed: trust, skills, lived experience, lower costs or access. For example: A co-founder grew up in the district and is trusted by local parents.

7
00:00:51.793 --> 00:01:05.804
Your choices: What you will not do, who you will not prioritise yet and what you refer to others. For example: No adult classes for now; adults are referred to the library’s evening course.

8
00:01:06.204 --> 00:01:06.804
Why it matters

9
00:01:06.804 --> 00:01:12.107
1. Saying no protects quality when time and money are limited.

10
00:01:12.107 --> 00:01:18.152
2. Partners can see where you fit and how to work with you.

11
00:01:18.152 --> 00:01:24.826
3. Funders and customers want to know why you, not someone else.

12
00:01:25.226 --> 00:01:25.826
What it guides

13
00:01:25.826 --> 00:01:30.389
1. Your strategic objectives: where to put effort first.

14
00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:34.952
2. Your brand and messages, later in the course.

15
00:01:34.952 --> 00:01:41.256
3. Turning down opportunities that pull you away from your gap.

16
00:01:41.656 --> 00:01:42.256
What to avoid

17
00:01:42.256 --> 00:01:47.189
Claiming “passion” or “innovation” without showing what they produce.

18
00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:51.011
Trying to serve everyone at once.

19
00:01:51.011 --> 00:01:56.944
Presenting advantages you still need to prove as facts.

20
00:01:57.544 --> 00:01:59.344
You write your positioning statement and the choices it implies.

21
00:01:59.344 --> 00:02:03.344
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:04.844 --> 00:02:07.944
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
